  "why": "The fourth review pass. Five export surfaces this pass does not read in full \u2014 `Object.freeze({\u2026})`, `module.exports = make()`, an alias assigned after its declaration, a subscript `exports['find']`, and `Object.assign` onto an alias \u2014 each of which the third pass still treated as readable and so enforced, dropping a true call. \"Readable\" is an allowlist now, and every one of these calls is resolved by name and kept because its target exists. Plus a renamed export, `{ Handler: Impl }`, with no class called `Handler` anywhere to hide behind, so the method call must be routed through the export map before the existence check rather than after it. Plus two bindings that shadow the module's `store` over their own scope only: a `var` inside a callback (hoisted to the callback, not to `go`) and a `catch (store)` clause. A scope that runs past either loses the true `store.find()` on the last line.",
